                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is Bewakoof's biggest moat?</h3>
                                        <p>Licensed IP partnerships (Marvel, DC, F.R.I.E.N.D.S, cricket teams) create built-in fandom + differentiation vs commodity fashion. Compounding advantage.</p>
                                        <h3>Bewakoof or The Souled Store — which is bigger?</h3>
                                        <p>Different segments. Bewakoof leans casual + affordable + humour. TSS leans premium + licensed IP + broader category (includes women's + accessories). Both meaningful.</p>
                                        <h3>Can new brands compete with Bewakoof?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes in premium (Snitch), heritage-casual (The Bear House), niche IP (regional cricket, gaming). Category niching works.</p>
                                        <h3>Is Bewakoof profitable?</h3>
                                        <p>Profitability trajectory common D2C consideration. Focus on unit economics + margin discipline vs volume-only scaling.</p>
